# The AI providers a development HQ starts with, so a wiped dev database does not mean typing every key again.
#
# Copy to `.env.dev` at the repository root and fill in what you have; it is gitignored. Read only by
# `hq/scripts/dev/add-providers.mjs`, which `hq/scripts/dev/start.sh` (and so `fresh.sh`) runs beside hq: once hq is
# up it adds each provider set here that the organisation does not have yet, through hq's control socket, as
# `provider add` does on an installed machine. Each key is checked with its vendor first, as in the screens; a provider
# already there is left as it is, so changing a key here does nothing until it is removed in Settings › Providers.
# Leave a value blank to skip it, and to go through adding that provider by hand (the setup flow, say).
#
# Never read by the apps or by any test, and never exported into the shell: the names carry `DEV_` so that sourcing
# this file by mistake cannot hand a key to a tool that reads `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` or `OPENAI_API_KEY`.
#
# The keeper of every value is the team's vault: `scripts/secrets/export-to-vault.sh .env.dev` after any change,
# `scripts/secrets/import-from-vault.sh .env.dev` on a new machine (`.env.vault` says where the vault is).
#
# Use keys of their own for development, named after it (e.g. `agenthix-dev`) and with a spending limit where the vendor
# offers one, never the keys a real HQ uses.

# --- Models (LLM) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider: OpenRouter, one key for many vendors' models, the baseline among them.
# Where to get it: OpenRouter › Settings › API Keys › Create key, with a credit limit. Shown once.
DEV_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Provider: Anthropic (the Claude API, billed per use; not a Claude subscription, which a person connects themselves).
# Where to get it: console.anthropic.com › Settings › API Keys › Create Key. Starts `sk-ant-`. Shown once.
DEV_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Provider: OpenAI.
# Where to get it: platform.openai.com › API keys › Create new secret key. Starts `sk-`. Shown once.
DEV_OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Provider: Google (Gemini, through the Gemini API).
# Where to get it: aistudio.google.com › Get API key › Create API key. Starts `AIza`.
DEV_GOOGLE_API_KEY=

# --- Voice -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Provider: AssemblyAI, speech to text.
# Where to get it: assemblyai.com › Dashboard › API Keys. Paste the key as shown, with no `Bearer` before it.
DEV_ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY=

# Provider: Inworld, text to speech.
# Where to get it: platform.inworld.ai › Settings › API Keys › Generate new key, then copy its **Basic (Base64)**
#   credential, the one already encoded (not the separate key and secret). Paste it with no `Basic ` before it.
DEV_INWORLD_API_KEY=
